---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InfoPage from '@/components/InfoPage.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="How We Choose Date Night Ideas" description="How Date Night Ideas researches, edits, filters, and recommends plans for couples." canonicalPath="/about">
  <InfoPage eyebrow="How it works" title="We turn a big list into three good calls." intro="The product is designed around a simple belief: more options are not useful when you are already tired of deciding.">
    <h2>Research broadly</h2><p>We review accessible public editorial guides and practical activity references to identify useful date concepts. Every source fetch records its status, title, access time, response size, and content hash; each Idea maps to two relevant sources.</p>
    <h2>Edit for a real night</h2><p>A title is not a plan. Every published Idea is independently rewritten with a concrete setup, realistic time and budget, three executable steps, a variation, an easier fallback, and a unique review record. We do not copy or lightly paraphrase source text.</p>
    <h2>Keep hard limits hard</h2><p>Alcohol-free, kid-friendly, indoor-only, low-prep, and public-friendly choices are filters, not suggestions. Soft preferences can relax if the catalog is thin; hard limits do not.</p>
    <h2>Explain the match</h2><p>Each result names the answers it fits. Recommendation rules use structured catalog fields rather than free-form text generation at runtime.</p>
    <h2>Use three as a finish line</h2><p>The result set is intentionally small. Refresh changes the shortlist without asking the questions again, but the interface never turns into another wall of options.</p>
  </InfoPage>
</BaseLayout>
